          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 06:38:24.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20791 efalnd: Destroy connections only from the daemon",
        "message": "LU-20791 efalnd: Destroy connections only from the daemon\n\nA connection establishment error destroyed the connection in place, on\nthe context that hit the error. The connection was already published in\nthe hash table and visible to concurrent lookups, so another context\ncould hold a reference and still be using it when it was freed, a\nuse-after-free. The reference count added to guard this was only honored\nby the cleanup daemon, not by these error paths.\n\nHave the error paths deactivate the connection instead of destroying it:\nunhash it and mark it for teardown, then leave the actual destroy to the\ndaemon, which already waits for the reference count to drain and the\ntransmit queues to empty. The daemon is now the only context that\ndestroys a published connection.\n\nDeactivation defers the cancellation of the connection's pending\ntransmits to the daemon, which previously cancelled them all with one\ngeneric status. Record the health status and errno on the connection\nwhen it is marked for teardown so the daemon can apply the specific\nreason the tearing-down context knew. The idle scanner stores an\naborted-on-timeout reason and a connection never torn down this way\nkeeps a benign default.\n\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nChange-Id: I1ad648221d02a279074f0b2ed01cf183f736ba52\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69936\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Zanhua Huang <zanhua@amazon.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
